      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Two fetched pages; RHS and MBG not fetched. NC State: keep consistently moist, not wet; prefers distilled or rain water (fluoride browns tips); bright indirect or partial shade; steady 65 to 75 F (18 to 24 C, converted), no minimum; humidity at least 60%; 2 to 3 ft tall, 1 to 2 ft wide; rapid growth; erect columnar clump. Humidity: page says at least 60%, a floor with no upper figure, and the schema stores a range, so left unknown. Toxicity: NC State tags non-toxic for cats and dogs; ASPCA agrees at genus level (Calathea spp.), so corroboration is genus-level. Base interval is a guess."
      },
